>>
Rule 1 (diag input must be 1d or 2d)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 3 (diag input must be 1-D or 2-D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 2
>>
Rule 4 (diagonal offset k must be within matrix dimensions for 2D input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ 0 - shape(v_1, 0) < v_2 ∧ v_2 < shape(v_1, 1))
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor must have a valid numerical or boolean dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 6 (all dimensions of the input tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
